  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **[**(1st number × 2) + 2nd number] ÷ 10 = 3rd number\n\nGiven : \n\n(10, 20, 4)\n\n[__**(10 × 2)**__ + 20] ÷ 10 = 4 \n\n__**[**____20____** + 20]**__ ÷ 10 = 4 \n\n__**40 ÷ 10**__ = 4\n\n4 = 4 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n(15, 30, 6) \n\n[__(15 × 2)__ + 30] ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__[____30____ + 30]__ ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__60 ÷ 10__ = 6\n\n6 = 6 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\nOption - (1) : (20, 40, 8) \n\n[__(20 × 2)__ + 40] ÷ 10 = 8\n\n__[____40____ + 40]__ ÷ 10 = 8\n\n__80 ÷ 10__ = 8\n\n**8 = 8 (LHS = RHS)**\n\nOption - (2) : (20, 30, 8)\n\n[__(20 × 2)__ + 30] ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__[____40____ + 30]__ ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__70 ÷ 10__ = 6\n\n7 ≠ 6 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption - (3) : (20, 40, 6)\n\n[__(20 × 2)__ + 40] ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__[____40____ + 40]__ ÷ 10 = 6\n\n__80 ÷ 10__ = 6\n\n8 ≠ 6 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption - (4) : (10, 40, 8) \n\n[__(10 × 2)__ + 40] ÷ 10 = 8\n\n__[____20____ + 40]__ ÷ 10 = 8\n\n__60 ÷ 10__ = 8\n\n7 ≠ 8 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, \"Option - (1)\" is the correct answer.",
